---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How do I contact Brian?",
    a: `<p>Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> to send a message. Brian usually responds
        within a day or two.</p>`
  },
  {
    q: "Where can I buy the books?",
    a: `<p>All twelve titles are on
        <a href="https://www.amazon.com/stores/Brian-J.-Mueller/author/B00JQMV412">Amazon</a>, and
        other online retailers carry them too. Local bookshops can usually order them for you.</p>`
  },
  {
    q: "Are the poems copyrighted?",
    a: `<p>Yes, every poem is under copyright — but almost all of them are shared under a Creative
        Commons licence, so you already have permission to do a good deal without asking.</p>
        <p>Poems in the <a href="/series/the-bull-series">Bull Series</a>,
        <a href="/series/poem-of-the-day">Brian's Poem of the Day</a>,
        <a href="/books/trust-stillness"><em>Trust Stillness</em></a>,
        <a href="/books/cock-a-doodle-doo"><em>Cock-A-Doodle-Doo</em></a> and the
        <a href="/series/men-writing-for-change">Men Writing for Change</a> volumes are licensed
        under a <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/">Creative Commons
        Attribution-NonCommercial-NoDerivatives 4.0 International License</a>.</p>
        <p>That covers all twelve books, <a href="/books/cock-a-doodle-doo"><em>Cock-A-Doodle-Doo</em></a>
        included. Its printed copyright page still carries the older, stricter notice; the Creative
        Commons licence above is the current one and it governs.</p>
        <p>The Men Writing for Change volumes gather poems written by the men who came to the
        retreats. Each of them granted Brian the copyright when the volume was published, which is
        why those poems sit under the same Creative Commons licence as everything else here —
        though they remain, and are credited as, the work of the men who wrote them.</p>`
  },
  {
    q: "What does that Creative Commons license let me do?",
    a: `<p>You are free to share, copy and redistribute the material in any medium or format,
        under three conditions:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Attribution</b> — give appropriate credit, link to the license, and say if you
              changed anything. Not in any way that suggests Brian endorses you or your use.</li>
          <li><b>NonCommercial</b> — you may not use the material commercially.</li>
          <li><b>NoDerivatives</b> — if you remix or build on it, you may not distribute the
              modified version.</li>
        </ul>`
  },
  {
    q: "Can I get permissions beyond that?",
    a: `<p>Often, yes. Permissions beyond the scope of the Creative Commons license or the
        traditional copyright may be available — <a href="/contact">write with your specific
        request</a>.</p>`
  },
];
---
<Base title="Questions — Brian J. Mueller"
      description="Buying the books, copyright and Creative Commons licensing, permissions, and how to reach Brian.">
  <section class="wrap stack stack-l">
    <div class="stack stack-m prose">
      <div class="eyebrow">Questions</div>
      <h1>Frequently asked</h1>
      <hr class="rule-short" />
      <p class="lede">The things people write in to ask most often.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq prose">
      {faqs.map(f => (
        <details>
          <summary>{f.q}</summary>
          <div class="faq-body" set:html={f.a} />
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
